  "title": "Bits see a three-manifold only through mod-2 cohomology",
  "subject": "What bits see of a three-manifold, natively and through hubs",
  "conclusion": "Native networks of a triangulation see only its dual graph, and among the 32,768 symmetric bit laws on edges only trivial and parity laws survive the 2-3 and 1-4 moves, so bits see a three-manifold only through hubs and then only through its mod-2 first cohomology. The Fibonacci rule, which sees surfaces exactly, needs a negative weight to see three-manifolds, so no count of hidden witnesses realizes it.",
